  <main class="main">
    <p class="subtitle">Everything you need to set up and use Misci.</p>

    <h2 id="installation">Installation</h2>
    <p>Download the latest release for your platform from <a href="https://github.com/notinvisible-dev/Misci-AI/releases">GitHub Releases</a>.</p>
    <p>Available for Linux (AppImage), Windows (portable .exe), and macOS.</p>
    <h3>Linux</h3>
    <pre><code><span class="prompt-char">$</span> chmod +x misci-desktop-*.AppImage
<span class="prompt-char">$</span> ./misci-desktop-*.AppImage --no-sandbox</code></pre>
    <h3>Windows</h3>
    <p>Run the portable <code>.exe</code> directly. No installation required.</p>
    <h3>macOS</h3>
    <p>Open the <code>.dmg</code> and drag Misci to your Applications folder.</p>

    <h2 id="configuration">Configuration</h2>
    <p>Misci reads from <code>opencode.json</code> or <code>opencode.jsonc</code> in your project root. The config file sets your providers, models, agents, and permissions.</p>
    <h3>Minimal config</h3>
    <pre><code>{
  "$schema": "https://opencode.ai/config.json",
  "provider": {
    "openai": {
      "api-key": "env:OPENAI_API_KEY"
    }
  }
}</code></pre>
    <div class="callout callout-info">
      <strong>Tip:</strong> Use <code>env:VARIABLE_NAME</code> to reference environment variables. Never hardcode API keys in your config file.
    </div>
    <h3>Config options</h3>
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Key</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><code>provider</code></td><td>LLM provider configuration and API keys</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>model</code></td><td>Default model for each provider</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>agent</code></td><td>Custom agent definitions</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>command</code></td><td>Custom slash commands</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>mcp</code></td><td>MCP server connections</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>permission</code></td><td>Tool permission rules</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <h2 id="providers">Providers</h2>
    <p>Misci supports all major LLM providers out of the box.</p>
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Provider</th><th>Key</th><th>Env variable</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>OpenAI</td><td><code>openai</code></td><td><code>OPENAI_API_KEY</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td>Anthropic</td><td><code>anthropic</code></td><td><code>ANTHROPIC_API_KEY</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td>Google</td><td><code>google</code></td><td><code>GOOGLE_API_KEY</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td>xAI</td><td><code>xai</code></td><td><code>XAI_API_KEY</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td>Mistral</td><td><code>mistral</code></td><td><code>MISTRAL_API_KEY</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td>OpenAI-compatible</td><td><code>openai-compatible</code></td><td>Custom URL + key</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <h3>Using multiple providers</h3>
    <pre><code>{
  "provider": {
    "openai": { "api-key": "env:OPENAI_API_KEY" },
    "anthropic": { "api-key": "env:ANTHROPIC_API_KEY" }
  },
  "model": {
    "default": "gpt-5",
    "big": "claude-opus-4-5"
  }
}</code></pre>

    <h2 id="desktop">Desktop App</h2>
    <p>The Misci desktop app bundles the full agent with a graphical interface, session management, and file tree navigation.</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Session management</strong> — Create, switch, and search sessions from the sidebar.</li>
      <li><strong>File tree</strong> — Browse your project files directly in the app.</li>
      <li><strong>Settings</strong> — Configure providers, models, and themes from the UI.</li>
      <li><strong>Permissions</strong> — Review and approve tool actions before they execute.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="keyboard">Keyboard shortcuts</h2>
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Shortcut</th><th>Action</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><code>Ctrl+Enter</code></td><td>Send message</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>Ctrl+N</code></td><td>New session</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>Ctrl+K</code></td><td>Quick search</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>Ctrl+,</code></td><td>Open settings</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>Esc</code></td><td>Cancel / close</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <h2 id="themes">Themes</h2>
    <p>Misci ships with 40+ built-in themes and adapts to your system's light or dark mode preference automatically.</p>
    <p>Apply themes from Settings, or create your own:</p>
    <pre><code>{
  "$schema": "https://opencode.ai/desktop-theme.json",
  "name": "My Theme",
  "colors": {
    "background": "#ffffff",
    "foreground": "#18181b",
    "accent": "#5b4ccc"
  }
}</code></pre>
    <p>Save your theme as a <code>.json</code> file and load it from the Settings panel.</p>

    <h2 id="skills">Built-in skills</h2>
    <p>Skills are specialized capabilities that Misci can use when relevant. They activate automatically based on your request.</p>
    <div class="callout callout-info">
      <strong>How it works:</strong> Misci reads your message, determines which skills are relevant, and activates them. You don't need to invoke skills manually.
    </div>

    <h3>Document skills</h3>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>PDF</strong> — Create, edit, merge, split, fill forms, encrypt/decrypt PDFs</li>
      <li><strong>PDF Reading</strong> — Read, extract text, tables, images, and perform OCR</li>
      <li><strong>DOCX</strong> — Create and edit Word documents with formatting</li>
      <li><strong>PowerPoint</strong> — Build and edit slide decks</li>
      <li><strong>Excel</strong> — Create, edit, format, and chart spreadsheets</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Creative skills</h3>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Algorithmic Art</strong> — Generate art with p5.js and seeded randomness</li>
      <li><strong>Canvas Design</strong> — Create visual art for PNG and PDF output</li>
      <li><strong>Frontend Design</strong> — Guidance for distinctive UI design</li>
      <li><strong>Theme Factory</strong> — Apply and generate themes for artifacts</li>
      <li><strong>Web Artifacts</strong> — Build React/HTML components with Tailwind</li>
      <li><strong>Slack GIF Creator</strong> — Create animated GIFs optimized for Slack</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Writing skills</h3>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Humanizer</strong> — Rewrite text to sound natural and non-AI</li>
      <li><strong>Setup Writing Style</strong> — Learn the user's voice and match it</li>
      <li><strong>Doc Co-authoring</strong> — Structured workflow for co-writing documentation</li>
      <li><strong>Internal Comms</strong> — Write status reports, updates, and newsletters</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Productivity skills</h3>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Financial Calculator</strong> — Tax estimates, loan comparisons, retirement projections</li>
      <li><strong>Event Planning</strong> — Venue research, guest lists, timelines, budgets</li>
      <li><strong>Morning Briefing</strong> — Daily news and weather briefing</li>
      <li><strong>YouTube Subtitles</strong> — Summarize YouTube videos via subtitles</li>
      <li><strong>Memory</strong> — Persist preferences and context across sessions</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Developer skills</h3>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>MCP Builder</strong> — Guide for building MCP servers</li>
      <li><strong>Skill Creator</strong> — Create, edit, and test custom skills</li>
      <li><strong>Criticize</strong> — Analyze weaknesses and provide concrete feedback</li>
      <li><strong>Learn</strong> — Structured teaching and concept explanation</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="custom-skills">Custom skills</h2>
    <p>Create your own skills by adding a Markdown file to your project's <code>.opencode/skills/</code> directory.</p>
    <pre><code>.opencode/
  skills/
    my-skill/
      SKILL.md</code></pre>
    <p>The <code>SKILL.md</code> file contains the skill's instructions. Misci loads it automatically when relevant.</p>
    <h3>Skill file format</h3>
    <pre><code># My Skill

Description of what this skill does and when to activate it.

## Instructions

Step-by-step guidance for the AI to follow.

## Examples

Example inputs and expected outputs.</code></pre>
    <div class="callout callout-warn">
      <strong>Note:</strong> Skill names are derived from the folder name. Use lowercase with hyphens (e.g., <code>my-cool-skill</code>).
    </div>

    <h2 id="mcp">MCP servers</h2>
    <p>Connect to Model Context Protocol servers to extend Misci with external tools and data sources.</p>
    <pre><code>{
  "mcp": {
    "my-server": {
      "command": "npx",
      "args": ["-y", "my-mcp-server"],
      "env": {
        "API_KEY": "env:MY_API_KEY"
      }
    }
  }
}</code></pre>
    <p>Misci will discover the tools exposed by each MCP server and make them available to the agent automatically.</p>

    <h2 id="agents">Custom agents</h2>
    <p>Define specialized agents for different workflows. Each agent has its own system prompt and model selection.</p>
    <pre><code>{
  "agent": {
    "reviewer": {
      "name": "Code Reviewer",
      "description": "Reviews code for bugs and style issues",
      "system": "You are a senior code reviewer. Focus on correctness, security, and maintainability.",
      "model": "claude-opus-4-5"
    }
  }
}</code></pre>

    <h2 id="commands">Commands</h2>
    <p>Custom slash commands give you quick access to repeated workflows.</p>
    <pre><code>{
  "command": {
    "test": {
      "description": "Run tests and fix failures",
      "system": "Run the test suite. If any tests fail, analyze the failure and fix the code. Run tests again to confirm."
    }
  }
}</code></pre>
    <p>Use it by typing <code>/test</code> in any session.</p>

